+
+    <aside class="blender-bridge"><div><span class="eyebrow">BACK IN THE REAL TOOLS</span><h2>Tileable textures in Photoshop and Blender</h2><p>The same steps as in this lab. Photoshop menus change little between versions; the Blender names are the ones in the Shader Editor and the UV Editor.</p></div><ol>
+      <li><strong>Photoshop:</strong> crop a square (Crop Tool, <strong>1:1 (Square)</strong>), then <strong>Image › Image Size</strong> to a power of two. Even out the light before anything else (a blurred, desaturated, inverted copy in <strong>Linear Light</strong> at 50 %, or a <strong>High Pass</strong>).</li>
